<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MAINE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Egg Rock Light (Maine) is a lighthouse on Frenchman Bay, Maine, built in 1875, and is one of coastal Maine's architecturally unique lighthouses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRENCHMAN BAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Frenchman Bay is a body of water in Maine where Egg Rock Light is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOUNT DESERT ISLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mount Desert Island is a location near Egg Rock Light, situated midway between Egg Rock and the Schoodic Peninsula."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SCHOODIC PENINSULA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Schoodic Peninsula is a location near Egg Rock Light, situated midway between Egg Rock and Mount Desert Island."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT STATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Egg Rock Light Station is a historic site consisting of two buildings, a combination light tower and keeper's house, and a fog station building."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL REGISTER OF HISTORIC PLACES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Register of Historic Places is an official list of the United States' historic places deemed worthy of preservation."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUG LIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bug Light, also known as Portland Breakwater Lighthouse, is a 26-foot, cast-iron lighthouse located at the entrance to Portland Harbor, Maine. It is not available to visit, but the grounds are."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORTLAND HARBOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Portland Harbor is a harbor in Maine where Bug Light is located."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEAR ISLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bear Island is mentioned as a previous location of a lighthouse before the construction of Egg Rock Light."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MASSACHUSETTS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Egg Rock Light (Massachusetts) is a lighthouse first established in 1856, located on an island, and was rebuilt with a square tower attached to the house after a fire in 1897."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHARK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The wreck of the schooner 'Shark' led to a change in the characteristic of Egg Rock Light from flashing to fixed red."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONG ISLAND HEAD LIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Long Island Head Light is a reference point that caused confusion with Egg Rock Light due to a reported incident involving the 'Shark' schooner."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1875&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1875 is the year when Egg Rock Light (Maine) was built."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1897&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1897 is the year when a fire occurred at Egg Rock Light (Massachusetts), leading to its rebuilding."&lt;SEP&gt;"1897 is the year when the former assistant keeper’s bedroom became a museum at Bug Light."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1904&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1904 is the year when the fog signal building was constructed."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1920&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1920 is the year when the present Egg Rock Light was constructed to replace the original structure."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1976&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1976 is the year when the Egg Rock Light was automated."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1856&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1856 is the year when Egg Rock Light (Massachusetts) was first established."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1988&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1988 is the year when Egg Rock Light Station was listed on the National Register of Historic Places."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;54 FEET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"54 feet is the height of the Bug Light."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;26 FEET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"26 feet is the height of the Bug Light."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRICK AND CAST-IRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brick and cast-iron are the materials used in the construction of Bug Light."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WHITE BRICK AND CAST-IRON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MATERIAL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"White brick and cast-iron are the materials used in the construction of Egg Rock Light (Maine)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;5 SECONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"5 seconds is the interval of the characteristic of the present Egg Rock Light, which flashes red every 5 seconds."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWO BLASTS EVERY 30 SECONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Two blasts every 30 seconds is the characteristic of the fog signal at Egg Rock Light."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MAINE)&quot;" target="&quot;FRENCHMAN BAY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Egg Rock Light (Maine) is located on Frenchman Bay, Maine."</data>
      <data key="d5">"location, navigation aid"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MAINE)&quot;" target="&quot;MOUNT DESERT ISLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Egg Rock Light (Maine) is located midway between Mount Desert Island and the Schoodic Peninsula."</data>
      <data key="d5">"proximity, navigation aid"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MAINE)&quot;" target="&quot;SCHOODIC PENINSULA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Egg Rock Light (Maine) is located midway between Mount Desert Island and the Schoodic Peninsula."</data>
      <data key="d5">"proximity, navigation aid"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MAINE)&quot;" target="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT STATION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Egg Rock Light Station consists of two buildings, a combination light tower and keeper's house, and a fog station building, which are part of Egg Rock Light (Maine)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"station, maintenance"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MAINE)&quot;" target="&quot;NATIONAL REGISTER OF HISTORIC PLACES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Egg Rock Light (Maine) was listed on the National Register of Historic Places as Egg Rock Light Station in 1988."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical significance, preservation"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BUG LIGHT&quot;" target="&quot;PORTLAND HARBOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bug Light is located at the entrance to Portland Harbor, Maine, and the grounds are accessible to visitors."</data>
      <data key="d5">"navigation aid, tourism"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEAR ISLAND&quot;" target="&quot;EGG ROCK LIGHT (MASSACHUSETTS)&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bear Island is mentioned as a previous location of a lighthouse before the construction of Egg Rock Light (Massachusetts)."</data>
      <data key="d5">"history, predecessor"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0193-013750095677</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
